Janis Papanagnou wrote:
>
> My chaotic priest is wielding Stormbringer. For apparent reasons I want to
> occasionally switch weapons. I've got a bunch of other artifacts and like
> to take one of them as secondary weapon. My skill to use the rustproof +3
> Excalibur and the corroded +0 Firebrand which I found in the dungeon lying
> around is still Restricted. I've got two more broadswords, the Orcrist and
> the Dragonbane (and I've stashed Sting and Trollbane). Those broadswords
> are not listed in the art2-343.txt, because they don't qualify as "worth
> keeping", as we can read. But I am reluctant to use one of the longsword
> artifacts; Excalibur blasts me and I've only about 100 HPs. Either way I
> can switch to Stormbringer as soon as necessary, but I want to choose the
> best secondary weapon for an accidental first hit and for the case that I
> play sloppily and forget to switch weapons; for that purpose I tend to use
> Dragonbane because those dragons are tough. Or use Excalibur as default?
> Other opinons?

Excalibur - Automatic searching is a huge advantage, blasting is a huge
disadvantage.  I would want it in a chest because of the risk of blasts.

Fire brand - Double damage against a large assortment of monsters is a
large advantage.  Once your luck is maxed out restricted skill no longer
matters.  I would begin to enchant this one and start using it at some
point.  Stays in the bag until switching to it.

Orcrist - By this time orcs are irrelevant, but its hard to damage this
wooden sword and elven broadsword is a better general weapon than a
regular broadsword.  Consider the non-artifact sorting of what weapon to
use - long sword, elven broadsword, broadsword, scimitar, silver saber. 
To me this says use Orcrist over Dragonbane based on their non-artifact
damage until Fire brand is enchanted.  Stays in open inventory until
switching to Fire brand.

Dragonbane - Dragons are rare so in most cases this is just a regular
broadsword.  In the chest based on my Orcrist comment.  Maybe not worth
pulling out of the stash even for Ludios - I might prefer the level
draining of Strombringer to the double damage of Dragonsbane.

Sting - For dagger classes it's a no-brainer win.  For restricted
classes it's just a non-stacking elven dagger with low weight and low
damage.  Into the chest unless you want it in your quiver.

Trollbane - I would consider it a rustproof mundane war hammer.  The bad
news is it's a war hammer and they are pitiful mundane weapons.  Unless
you get Mjollnir somehow the worse news is you're allowed to waste skill
slots on it all the way up to Expert.  Into the chest to avoid the
temptation.

Without maxed luck and high enchantment I'd go with Orcrist because
dragons are so rare.  I would spend my ?oEW on Fire brand, though. 
Switch to it once it's +2 or better and you have max luck to overcome
the restriction.  Early on Stormbringer primary, Orcrist secondary wield
with Sting in the quiver.  Later on Stormbringer primary, Fire brand
secondary wield with a stack of highly enchanted non-artifact elven
daggers in the quiver.  Going with bow is unlikely to be worth the
disappearing arrows.


